WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.532
I need the Department of Higher Education.

00:00:02.692 --> 00:00:03.609
Tab to About.

00:00:03.769 --> 00:00:04.498
Down arrow.

00:00:04.658 --> 00:00:05.737
Where did the link go?

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.458
I turn on Curb Cut.

00:00:08.618 --> 00:00:09.429
Same menu.

00:00:09.589 --> 00:00:10.552
Same keyboard.

00:00:10.712 --> 00:00:11.409
There it is.

00:00:11.569 --> 00:00:12.435
The DHE.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.319
Kane tries the same task with a mouse.

00:00:17.479 --> 00:00:19.086
The department page opens.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.716
With keys alone, Kane cannot reach that link.

00:00:23.876 --> 00:00:25.833
Now we have a reproducible failure.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.132
Here’s a failure that went straight back to the coding agent.

00:00:30.292 --> 00:00:32.047
Watch the converter’s answer field.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.404
At this width, the field runs off the screen.

00:00:35.564 --> 00:00:39.975
Codex receives Kane’s failed assertion and writes a rule to stack the cells.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:43.322
Kane runs it again.

00:00:43.482 --> 00:00:44.217
One meter.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.590
The answer is visible.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:50.284
At Munich Airport, listen to the previous slide control.

00:00:50.444 --> 00:00:50.890
[Reading voice] Button.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.234
[Reading voice] Vorherige Folie.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.559
On Meridiano, two buttons have no names.

00:00:56.719 --> 00:00:59.068
TypeSafe Jev names them in about a second.

00:00:59.228 --> 00:00:59.584
[Reading voice] Menú.

00:00:59.744 --> 00:01:00.274
[Reading voice] Buscar.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:07.681
The site owner gets the task, the recordings, and a source repair.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.110
One hundred five fixes are live.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.632
Get Curb Cut for Chrome.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.638
On ExtremeTerrain, the Details link is faint.

00:01:17.798 --> 00:01:20.697
Curb Cut adjusts its contrast and measures the result.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.167
Let’s look at what Kane actually checked.

00:01:23.327 --> 00:01:27.212
On Mass.edu, the target is a specific department page.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:32.153
The tester gets a keyboard and the same destination.

00:01:32.313 --> 00:01:34.049
Down arrow leaves About focused.

00:01:34.209 --> 00:01:35.829
The link underneath stays hidden.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:40.723
In the pointer control, hover reveals the link.

00:01:40.883 --> 00:01:43.778
Following it confirms that the destination exists.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:49.607
The installed rule gives focus the same behavior as hover.

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:52.803
With that rule, Kane follows the link using only keys.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:58.858
For the converter, we can trace the handoff to a single failed run.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:03.713
Its identifier travels with the assertion into the coding agent’s repair record.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:10.298
The agent changes the layout of the table and its cells.

00:02:10.458 --> 00:02:13.535
Now the result fits a three hundred twenty pixel viewport.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:18.071
For developers, curbcut check is the entry point.

00:02:18.231 --> 00:02:23.607
The intended loop runs the task, gives the agent Kane’s reason, and tests its next change.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:31.062
curbcut gate brings the same check into a coding agent’s stop hook.

00:02:31.222 --> 00:02:33.933
A failing task sends the agent back to the source.

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:43.875
In the trust popup, the visitor can inspect the verification status and play the supporting recording.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.883
Jev’s public test found names on seven sites.

00:02:49.043 --> 00:02:52.018
Thirteen of fifteen applied names were judged correct.

00:02:52.178 --> 00:02:53.160
Two were too vague.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:00.960
A visitor can report another barrier from the keyboard, at the point where the task breaks.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:09.200
For the About menu, the report recommends applying the hover styling when focus moves inside the menu.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:10.883
The owner can fix the source.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.460
The nightly local check repeats the task.

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:17.696
Public Kane rechecks also run without and with the patch.

00:03:17.856 --> 00:03:21.210
An inconclusive run preserves the last verified state.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:25.748
Once the unpatched task passes, Curb Cut retires its rule.

00:03:25.908 --> 00:03:28.271
The site now carries the repair for everyone.

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:31.871
Install Curb Cut for Chrome.

00:03:32.031 --> 00:03:36.297
Open the proof for a fix, replay the task, and see where your next key takes you.
